<section id="lanes" class="feature" aria-labelledby="lanes-title">
  <div class="section-heading copy">
    <h2 id="lanes-title">One project. Several running copies.</h2>
    <p>
      A lane groups the services and configuration for one running stack. Use separate worktrees,
      another checkout, or the same checkout with different settings.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="lane-details">
    <article class="copy">
      <h3>Ports that don't collide.</h3>
      <p>
        Each lane gets its own port range and local hostnames. Run checkout next to main without
        editing a pile of <code>.env</code> files.
      </p>
      <code class="example">
        main :20000
        <br />
        checkout :21000
      </code>
    </article>
    <article class="copy">
      <h3>Shared infra. Separate data.</h3>
      <p>
        Reuse infrastructure such as Postgres while giving each lane its own database. Try a
        migration without changing main's data.
      </p>
      <code class="example">
        postgres / myapp_main
        <br />
        postgres / myapp_lane1
      </code>
    </article>
    <article class="copy">
      <h3>Your stack, described once.</h3>
      <p>
        A project configuration describes services, environment variables and lifecycle tasks. Each
        lane gets the values it needs.
      </p>
      <code class="example">
        devlanes.yaml
        <br />
        web + api + worker
      </code>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
